    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "34e5aa3b-db10-40a1-893d-79e98cd3f2f4",
      "key": "3a80200d-d68f-4fe0-a06e-ae514d70d8eb",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Features"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E4* hotel\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHalf board accommodation\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAll excursions \u0026amp; guided tours included\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBlue Badge guide Days 2 to 4\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EExecutive coach throughout\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EOne free place per 10 paying passengers\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "1d09b5af-b95a-4af5-b8f2-323db029e817",
      "key": "aae571be-e223-4c2d-96f5-2228350fcb68",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Accommodation"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EFour nights on half board basis at the 4* Mercure Dunkenhalgh Hotel and Spa on the outskirts of Blackburn. Facilities at the hotel include a restaurant and bar and all rooms are en suite.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "2d9b0603-29ef-423a-8d3e-d9c039d3d7b1",
      "key": "ef3bd203-cd83-429e-aa5e-6bf03a549371",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Sights"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ELittle Moreton Hall\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ESkipton\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECruise on Leeds Liverpool Canal\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EGawthorpe Hall\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ELake Windermere cruise\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETrain ride on Lakeside \u0026amp; Haverthwaite Steam Railway\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ESizergh Castle \u0026amp; Gardens\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EGuided tour of Pendle Witch Country\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EClitheroe\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ERufford Old Hall\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EQuarry Bank Mill \u0026amp; Styal Estate\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "de535189-b468-4594-8118-f303bac50e3c",
      "key": "13ffc25d-4e61-4c76-a8af-22bb1054a489",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Tailor your sights"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETrain excursion on the Settle to Carlisle Railway - England\u2019s most scenic railway passes through the lush green Eden Valley with its stunning views of the Pennines and Lakeland Fells, before reaching the magnificent landscape of the Yorkshire Dales\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHolker Hall - home to the Cavendish family, this grand Victorian mansion is lavishly furnished, with marble fireplaces, splendid linenfold panelling, fine plasterwork and intricate carving\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ERHS Garden Bridgewater - a stunning new 156 acre garden created in the heart of the North West brings back to life the lost historic grounds at Worsley New Hall in Salford\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Here are some more suggested places of interest you might like to include:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "837beecf-4239-4b3d-b683-1d611af3da2e",
      "key": "63f11612-cd18-46d9-b2b8-d6b5db1beda5",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Ch3\u003EDay 1 \u2013 Little Moreton Hall\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EBoard our private executive coach at your preferred pick up points \u2013 visit a carefully selected National Trust property en route such as Little Moreton Hall in Cheshire, begun in 1504 and completed 100 years later and regarded as the finest example of a timber-framed moated house in the country \u2013 check in at the 4* Mercure Dunkenhalgh Hotel and Spa on the outskirts of Blackburn.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 2 \u2013 Skipton, Leeds Liverpool Canal \u0026amp; Gawthorpe Hall\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003ETime at leisure to explore Skipton, known as \u2018The Gateway to the Dales\u2019 \u2013 60 minute cruise on the Leeds Liverpool Canal to see Skipton and the surrounding countryside from a different perspective \u2013 the National Trust\u2019s Gawthorpe Hall set in the heart of urban Lancashire contains fabulously opulent interiors created by Sir Charles Barry in the 19th century.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 3 \u2013 Lake Windermere cruise, Lakeside \u0026amp; Haverthwaite Steam Railway \u0026amp; Sizergh Castle and Gardens\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EOne way cruise from Bowness to Lakeside affording us wonderful views of Lake Windermere and its shores \u2013 a journey on the Lakeside \u0026amp; Haverthwaite Steam Railway takes us through the Levan Valley, one of the Lake District\u2019s most beautiful \u2013 the National Trust\u2019s Sizergh Castle and Gardens is a medieval house extended in Elizabethan times and surrounded by beautiful grounds.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 4 \u2013 Guided tour of Pendle Witch Country, Clitheroe \u0026amp; Rufford Old Hall\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EA guided tour of Pendle Witch Country, famous for its grimly fiendish association with the Witches of Pendle and the famous witch trials in 1612 \u2013 visit the beautiful village of Downham, where \u2018Whistle Down the Wind\u2019, and \u2018Born and Bred\u2019 were filmed, and continue to the Pendle Heritage Centre and Museum, dedicated to the history and heritage of Pendle, and the story of the Pendle Witches \u2013 time at leisure for lunch in Clitheroe \u2013 the National Trust\u2019s Rufford Old Hall, home to the Hesketh family for almost 500 years and one of Lancashire\u2019s finest Tudor buildings, was built in the 1530\u2019s.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 5 \u2013 Quarry Bank Mill and Styal Estate\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe National Trust\u2019s Quarry Bank Mill and Styal Estate near Wilmslow is a restored Georgian cotton mill telling the story of \u2018King Cotton\u2019 from a bale of raw cotton to finished cloth, and the original Apprentice House recreates the 1830s atmosphere of the lives of child workers.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Suggested Itinerary"
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Every one of our tours is exclusively for your group and your group alone so each one can be tailor made to suit the interests and profile of your members until you have a tour with an itinerary and at a price which matches the interests and profile of your members."
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureSummary",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "Remember this itinerary is just our suggestion. "
          }
        }
      ]
    },
